# R3-EARTH-LINK EL3b (design r3/earth-link.md EL3b; Mark, attended 2026-10-28: "go ahead and we will
# start seeding the library - this is something that can build up over playthroughs"): the comms feed's
# shipped picture library, the seed of the library that later grows from painted-live frames. One
# picture per event of sim/data/feed_events.ail (48 events, six categories), pictures/<id>_v<k>.webp;
# this first seed is v0 for every event. events.json (here) holds each event's scene paragraph and the
# shared style block; the feed draws an event per Earth week and shows the event's pictures (a library
# frame; design EL3b "The feed is a mix"). The feed shows home's own news only: nothing from the ship.
# Generated 2026-10-28 by Codex imagegen (driver env -u OPENAI_API_KEY codex exec -m gpt-6.1-sol,
# codex-cli 0.164.0; image model id not exposed), every call with one style reference
# (assets/characters/medic/portrait_medic_y0_neutral.png, sha256 93a02944...0017, style only), in the
# look and town of the crossing review's home pictures (data/interlude/home). Every candidate was
# inspected at full frame and in four 768x512 quadrants at 1:1 for text-like marks and the rules;
# 61 candidates, 48 kept, 13 rejected and regenerated. Full provenance, every prompt verbatim and the
# rejected candidates: generation_notes.md (here).
#
# D-18 (big assets stay out of git): the masters are the generator's 1536x1024 RGB PNGs, byte for byte;
# kept in the public bucket at gs://stapledons-voyage-assets/feed/<master sha256>.png (published 2026-10-28,
# the URL ends each row). The game ships lossy WebP downscaled to 1024x683, made
# with:
#   cwebp -q 85 -m 6 -sharp_yuv -metadata none -resize 1024 0 <master>.png -o <id>_v0.webp   (libwebp 1.6.0)
# about 11 MB for the 48. The game crops the centre 16:9; the prompts keep everything important out of
# the top and bottom tenth.
# Format: <id>_v<k>.webp sha256 <webp> <- master sha256 <png>
